{
  "_comment": "The Grouped rows of the coverage matrix. The config files are organised by ARRAY STYLE (scalar / dot-product / sub-array / sub-array dot-product) and each holds both fabrics, so the row's \"case\" is what picks the Grouped entries out of them — no config file has to be duplicated per case. Each pair's K is exactly one contraction pass: a no-accumulator array emits one partial sum per pass and has nothing to sum them with.",
  "name": "grouped",
